 ## Background
-Originated in the "City-on-Web" paper, which addresses real-time neural rendering of large-scale scenes on the web [S1]. The method was developed to overcome specific web platform constraints, particularly the limit of ~16 texture units per shader [S1]. It draws inspiration from traditional graphics techniques for Level-of-Detail (LOD) generation [S1].
+Originated in the "City-on-Web" paper [S1]. The method addresses challenges associated with resource-independent block-based rendering on the web, specifically the limitation on the number and resolution of texture units that can be loaded into a shader [S1]. It draws inspiration from traditional graphics techniques for Level-of-Detail (LOD) generation [S1].
 
